# Virgil — Output Connectors

> **Setup**: copy this file to `config/connectors.md` and customize if you want to change where Virgil's outputs go.
> ```bash
> cp config/connectors.md.example config/connectors.md
> ```

Defines where Virgil's outputs are routed. Each output has a default destination that can be reconfigured per-instance.

---

## Output Contracts

| Output | Description | Default Destination | Binding |
|--------|------------|-------------------|---------|
| Daily Recap | End-of-day summary of wins, themes, carry-overs | Agent Updates DB (Notion) | `mcp__notion__API-post-page` with data_source_id from `user.md` |
| Task Creation | New tasks routed from input | Task Planner (Notion) | Local MCP `API-post-page` or curl fallback |
| Task Completion | Marking tasks as Done | Task Planner (Notion) | Local MCP `API-patch-page` or curl fallback |
| Daily Note | Raw capture log + curated narrative | Vault `Daily Notes/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | Filesystem write |
| Archive Note | Labelled, processed notes | Vault `Archive/` | Filesystem write |
| Knowledge Graph | Concept extraction from Writings/Thoughts | Optional separate vault + Ideas DB | Filesystem + Notion |
| Fallback Queue | Failed task-manager API calls | Vault `_notion_queue.md` | Filesystem write |

---

## How to Reconfigure

To change where an output goes (e.g., daily recap via email instead of Notion):

1. Update the binding in this file.
2. Ensure the target MCP server or API is available in `.mcp.json` (referenced from `user.md`).
3. Update the relevant `skills/<name>/SKILL.md` step that produces the output.

The skill files reference `config/connectors.md` for routing decisions. The skills define *what* is produced; this file defines *where* it goes.

---

## Alternative destinations (examples)

| Output | Alternative | What you'd need |
|--------|-------------|-----------------|
| Daily Recap | Email | SMTP server config or an email-MCP |
| Task Creation | Any task manager (Todoist, Linear, Things) | That tool's API + an MCP wrapper |
| Daily Note | Any markdown folder (Obsidian, Logseq, plain folder) | Just a filesystem path |
| Knowledge Graph | Disable entirely | Remove the Knowledge Distillation Pipeline section from `memory.md` |
